{%- comment -%}
  Product card.

  Params:
    product   (required)
    score     optional int — somm match strength for the active food filter
    why       optional string — the somm's one-line reason for this filter
    is_pick   optional bool — flag this card as "The pick"
    dim       optional bool — fade cards that don't answer the question
    show_add  optional bool — render an AJAX add button
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `render` cannot be used inside a {% liquid %} tag — it is a standalone tag
  only. Doing so breaks the whole template, which is why every product-bearing
  page 404'd while the 404 and page templates rendered fine.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture code %}{% render 'non-code', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign code = code | strip
  assign tastes = product.metafields.custom.profile | metafield_text | default: product.metafields.custom.tastes | metafield_text
  assign sits = product.metafields.custom.sits | metafield_text
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

<div
  class="non-card{% if dim %} non-card--dim{% endif %}"
  data-non-code="{{ code | escape }}"
  {% if score %}data-score="{{ score }}"{% endif %}>
  {%- comment -%}
    Sold out has to be legible from the shelf, not only from the button.

    A sold-out card already rendered a disabled "Sold out" button, but that is
    the last line of a card and it only appears when show_add is on — so the
    Cap and the Beanie, both at 0 with inventory policy DENY, read as ordinary
    products until you got to the bottom of them. The badge sits on the
    photograph where "The pick" sits, so the state is carried by the card
    itself. "The pick" wins if a card is somehow both, since a sold-out pick
    is not a pick.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if is_pick -%}
    <span class="non-card__flag">The pick</span>
  {%- elsif product.available == false -%}
    <span class="non-card__flag non-card__flag--out">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="non-card__media" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      {{
        product.featured_image
        | image_url: width: 800, format: 'webp'
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'lazy',
          widths: '300,400,600,800',
          sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 50vw',
          alt: product.featured_image.alt
          | default: product.title
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'non-card__placeholder' }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>

  <span class="non-card__code">{{ code }}</span>
  <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="non-card__name">{{ product.title }}</a>

  <span class="non-card__note">
    {%- comment -%}
      "Drinks like a dry rosé." — a sentence, not the fragment custom.sits
      holds. See snippets/drinks-like.liquid for what was wrong and why the
      wording is "drinks like" rather than "tastes like".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture drinks_like %}{% render 'drinks-like', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- if drinks_like != blank -%}
      {{ drinks_like | strip }} &middot;
    {%- elsif tastes != blank -%}
      {{ tastes }} &middot;
    {%- endif -%}
    {{ product.price | money }}
  </span>

  {%- if why != blank -%}
    <p class="non-card__why">{{ why }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if show_add -%}
    {%- if product.available -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="non-card__add"
        data-non-add
        data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}">
        Add
      </button>
    {%- else -%}
      <button type="button" class="non-card__add" disabled>{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</button>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
